# SABOTAGE: the HOST WIRING of per-org provisioning. `Samen.Web.OrgProvisioning` runs a host's
# per-org setup when a tenant org is CREATED (self-serve signup + the operator plane's New-account
# write); this host's hook is `Samenerp.Seeds.ensure_notes_search_index!/1`, wired at exactly one
# line in `config/config.exs`. This patch deletes that ONE config line and nothing else.
#
# What it refutes is the claim that a NEW org is provisioned at creation. Every creation path
# still works (an account is created, the redirect is the same), and the registry rows are still
# written by the seed backfill — so only the test that drives a real `POST /signup` and then asks
# the new org's `/pages?q=` for its own block can see the difference. That is the whole point:
# mounting a surface is not making it searchable, and an unregistered org's empty result set is
# indistinguishable from "nothing matches".
#
# NOT TOUCHED, deliberately: `Samen.Web.OrgProvisioning` itself (the seam, its fail-honest
# reporting, its `Mount.otp_app/1` resolution), the controller/LiveView call sites, and
# `Samenerp.Seeds.backfill_notes_search_index!/0` (the deploy-time repair). Removing the seam
# would fail four tests and tell us less about which link broke.
#
# No warning is introduced: the hooks list simply becomes empty, and `OrgProvisioning.configured?/1`
# is a legitimate `false` for a host that wires nothing (the framework default).
# APP: samenerp
# TEST_FILES: test/notes_org_provisioning_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: SIGNUP provisions the new org: exactly Doc.title + DocBlock.text, with no seed call
--- a/samenerp/config/config.exs
+++ b/samenerp/config/config.exs
@@ -276,7 +276,6 @@
 # `Samenerp.Seeds.seed!/0,1` backfills orgs that predate this wiring on every boot. The hook is
 # idempotent and guard-first: `SearchIndexGuard` refuses the vaulted `text_secure` column, so a
 # searchable Pages surface can never mean an indexed vault.
-config :samenerp, :org_provisioning, [{Samenerp.Seeds, :ensure_notes_search_index!, []}]
 
